  "content": {
    "id": "p36-q5-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "5",
    "prompt": "The quadrilateral $ABCD$ has its vertices on a circle with centre $O$. The diagonal $AB$ is a diameter of the circle and $AC=BD$. Prove that $AD=BC$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\triangle ACB\\cong\\triangle BDA$ (RHS), so $AD=BC$.",
      "worked": "$\\angle ACB=\\angle BDA=90^\\circ$ (angles in a semicircle).\n\nIn right triangles $ACB$ and $BDA$, $AB=BA$ (common hypotenuse) and $AC=BD$ (given). Thus $\\triangle ACB\\cong\\triangle BDA$ (RHS).\n\nTherefore $BC=AD$ (matching sides).",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
